920: ## 7. Edge Cases, Boundary Handling & TV Ergonomics
921: 
922: ### 7.1 Dead Ends vs Wrapping Policy
923: - **Horizontal Shelves**: At the boundary (e.g. Card 1 pressing Left, or last card pressing Right), navigation **must not wrap around**. Wrapping horizontally on a carousel is disorienting for TV users. The engine stops, emits `'deadend'`, and preserves focus.
924: - **Header Pill**: Left/Right navigates between Home, Movies, Series, and Search. It halts at boundaries (no circular wrapping).
925: - **Vertical Movement at Page Top**: Pressing Up from the topmost row in a view moves into the floating header. Pressing Up while focused on the header halts (dead end).
926: 
927: ### 7.2 Asymmetric Layout Transitions
928: - **Header Pill $(x \approx 800)$ to Content Hero $(x \approx 96)$**:
929:   Handled by the **Two-Pass Cone Evaluation** (§2.3). Pass 1 checks the $60^\circ$ cone; if no element is directly below the header pill, Pass 2 evaluates the full downward half-plane, smoothly landing on the Hero "Play Now" button.
930: - **Split Action Button Group**:
931:   "Details" and "My List" buttons are nested side-by-side within `.split-action-group`. When focused on "Play Now" and moving Right, edge-to-edge distance selects "Details". Moving Right again selects "My List". Moving Left reverses the sequence deterministically.
932: - **Virtual Keyboard Spacebar**:
933:   The Spacebar spans multiple columns. Moving Down from any key above the Spacebar's horizontal extent computes a positive X-projection overlap ($\text{overlap}_{\text{orth}} > 0$), routing directly into the Spacebar.
934: 
935: ### 7.3 Performance on webOS Hardware (LG 32LR686BPSA)
936: The target TV hardware features an ARM processor running webOS 8.5. To ensure a solid 60 FPS without layout thrashing:
937: 1. `getBoundingClientRect()` calls are performed only upon D-pad keydown events (not on continuous polling).
938: 2. Visibility checks use fast property lookups (`offsetParent`, `width`, `height`) before invoking `window.getComputedStyle()`.
939: 3. Focus classes utilize hardware-accelerated CSS properties (`transform`, `box-shadow`) promoted to independent GPU composite layers (`transform: translateZ(0)`).
940: 
